CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer vzalloc(sizeof(*list)...) over vzalloc(sizeof(struct hiddev_list)...)
#81: FILE: drivers/hid/usbhid/hiddev.c:282:
+	list = vzalloc(sizeof(struct hiddev_list));

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

